    "narrative": "Our core offensive output today is anchored by **James Wood**, who posts the highest efficiency rating (77.07) against Adrian Houser. His placement in the leadoff spot combined with an elite 0.404 xwOBA makes him our primary engine for Runs. **Josh Naylor** (76.33) and **Seiya Suzuki** (73.54) follow closely as high-ceiling plays; **Josh Naylor** benefits significantly from a favorable park factor and a manageable matchup against Rogers, while **Seiya Suzuki** capitalizes on a high SP_xERA for Sugano, turning his projection into a high-tier start. **Max Muncy** (66.89) is also worth highlighting as our most productive infielder, as he exploits a soft matchup against Robert Gasser to provide reliable power production.\n\nWe face a difficult decision at the margins, with **Kyle Karros** being the most difficult bench omission today. Despite his 52.46 score and favorable park, he ultimately fell short of the starting threshold due to a lack of elite sprint speed and a neutral platoon matchup against Colin Rea compared to our higher-upside starters. Meanwhile, **Travis Bazzana** remains a volatile play; while his 57.55 score merits inclusion, he bears a 43% rain risk and faces a challenging arm in Cole. **Gabriel Moreno** sits at the bottom of our start list (50.97), and while he is currently in the lineup, we will be monitoring the waiver wire for more efficient depth to ensure we are maximizing our daily game caps. **Dalton Rushing** remains glued to the bench today with a score of 35.62, failing to meet our floor requirements primarily due to a brutal matchup against Skenes and poor wind conditions.",
